<!-- Purpose: per-agent identity + goals config template — every agent in the platform gets one filled copy (gitignored where it contains anything not yet public, e.g. an unannounced agent name), read by identity/standup/retro/trust-ladder. -->

# Agent config: {agent-name}

Copy this file to `agent.md` inside the agent's own scope config directory (e.g. `packs/recruiting/config/agent.md`) and fill every field before the scope goes live. Do not leave placeholders in a production config.

## Identity

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Name | {e.g. "Aria"} — the public name used in every signature, mailbox display name, and Slack handle. Founder-approved (PRD §11 open question 2), never picked unilaterally by the agent. |
| Role | {e.g. "Recruiting agent"} |
| Mailbox | {e.g. recruiting@otpless.com} |
| Slack handle | {e.g. @aria-recruiting} |
| Department channel | {e.g. #hiring} |
| Calendar | {agent's own calendar, e.g. recruiting@otpless.com calendar} |
| Notion machine user | {agent's own Notion integration user, distinct from any human's} |
| GitHub account | {agent's own GitHub account for playbook PRs, per retro skill} |
| Manager (human accountable) | {name + role, e.g. "Satyam, Founder" — the human who reviews this agent's PRs, self-reviews, and incidents} |

## Goals (the numbers this agent owns)

List every number this agent is responsible for, with current target. Update targets as phases change; keep history in git, don't just overwrite silently for anything that affects a standup comparison.

| Metric | Target | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| {e.g. First response time to new applicant} | {e.g. < 24h} | |
| {e.g. Draft-acceptance rate (overall)} | {e.g. ≥ 80%} | Universal quality metric — every agent tracks this per action-class too |
| {e.g. Pipeline depth per open role} | {e.g. ≥ 10} | |
| {add rows per department pack} | | |

## Action-class autonomy levels (trust ladder — see packs/shared/trust-ladder/SKILL.md)

One row per distinct action-class this agent performs. Level changes only via a merged PR against `platform/deploy-layer/otpless/command-policy.md`, never edited here directly as a shortcut.

| Action-class | Current level | Evidence window | Last incident | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| {e.g. Scheduling confirmations} | L0 | — | — | Candidate for L1 once 2 weeks of data exists |
| {e.g. Application acknowledgments} | L0 | — | — | |
| {e.g. Outreach (new)} | L0 | — | — | Never above L0 without a human review step per playbook |
| {e.g. Applied-stage rejection} | L0 | — | — | Candidate for L2 per §trust-ladder, not before 4-week clean window |
| Offers / comp / terminations / performance judgments / post-interview rejections / policy changes | NEVER DELEGATED | n/a | n/a | Hard-coded deny in command policy regardless of any row above |

## Standup / retro cadence

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Daily standup time | 08:30 IST |
| Weekly self-review day | {e.g. Friday} |
| Weekly retro cron day | {e.g. Sunday night, ahead of Monday ops review} |
